Payload bundle: the bundle flag writes a copy of this binary with a makefile program in
its payload, as __main__.mk, and any further files, or every file under a further
directory, under their own relative names. The
zip is edited in place of a rebuild: everything ahead of the central directory is kept,
the new members are appended stored, and a new directory drops any member they replace.
A binary whose payload holds __main__.mk runs it when the caller names no makefile, as
if given -f with that member and -I with the payload root, so no shell is involved.

--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
